<title>BRAZIL: Brazil CSN launches $300 mln export notes.</title>
<headline>Brazil CSN launches $300 mln export notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian steelmaker Companhia Siderurgica Nacional (CSN) said it privately placed $300 million in fixed-rate and variable notes backed by export receivables via lead manager Chase Securities of New York.</p>
<p>The notes were rated an investment-grade BBB by Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co.</p>
<p>CSN said $160 million of the issue was in fixed-rate securities with the following terms:</p>
<p>YIELD: 225 basis points above comparable U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>AMORTIZATION PERIOD: seven years</p>
<p>GRACE PERIOD OF THE PRINCIPAL: one year.</p>
<p>INTEREST PAYMENT (monthly): Beginning Oct 15, 1996.</p>
<p>AMORTIZATION PAYMENT (monthly): Beginning Oct 15, 1997</p>
<p>The remaining $140 million was issued in variable notes with the following terms:</p>
<p>YIELD: 185 basis points over one-month Libor.</p>
<p>AMORTIZATION PERIOD: five years</p>
<p>GRACE PERIOD OF THE PRINCIPAL: one year.</p>
<p>INTEREST PAYMENT (monthly): Beginning Oct 15, 1996.</p>
<p>AMORTIZATION PAYMENT (monthly): Beginning Oct 15, 1997</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2324411</p>
